Model weights
-------------
The weights are not stored in this repository. `cargo run -p lightvc-xtask -- package`
copies three exported parts into models/ of the distribution:

  - models/front_gate — front end v4_dual (fixed mel filterbank, DCT matrix and
    causal dual pitch tracker; signal processing) plus a gate network and a
    time-frequency mask network with instantaneous mask activation
    (checkpoint snv_p126_gate_i80: gate from snv_p40_gate_t80, mask from snv_p45_mask).
    Trained on mixtures of
      - speech generated with Irodori-TTS-v4.1-Small (Aratako; MIT) by the fictional
        voices described below, and versions of that speech re-synthesized with
        WORLD (M. Morise; modified BSD) at lower pitch and longer vocal tract,
        passed through simulated recording chains and MP3 coding, and
      - real non-speech audio (music, noise, hand and object sounds) from MUSAN,
        the Free Music Archive and FSD50K (development split), limited to CC0,
        Public Domain and CC BY sources with speech removed. The per-source credits
        are listed in ATTRIBUTION_SOURCES.md. No source audio is distributed.

  - models/k3g — three content encoders and circuits whose outputs are averaged
    (checkpoints snv_p125a_c, snv_p125b_c and snv_p125e_c; the frame-wise weights
    and the attention keys and values are stored as 16-bit floats). Trained only on
    speech generated with Irodori-TTS-v4.1-Small (Aratako; MIT): 564 fictional voices
    (VoiceDesign, made from text descriptions; no recording of a real person was used
    as a voice reference), 10 utterances per voice, non-verbal vocalizations by the
    same voices, and the same sentences read by different voices; the encoders also
    saw WORLD re-synthesized and recording-chain versions of that speech.
    The sentences were taken from the transcripts of a non-public speech dataset,
    which is not distributed.

  - models/rvoc3hi — vocoder snv_p123_s (step 20000), fine-tuned from rvoc3hi
    (step 330000) on speech and non-verbal vocalizations generated with
    Irodori-TTS-v4.1-Small (Aratako; MIT) by the 564 fictional voices above.
    The base checkpoint rvoc3hi (step 330000) was trained on:
      - a non-public dataset of real speech, which is not distributed;
      - speech generated with Irodori-TTS-600M-v3-VoiceDesign (Aratako; MIT)
        using clips of that dataset as voice references.

Bundled voice presets
---------------------
voices/ holds 30 target voice references (15 female, 15 male; one FLAC file per
voice, 48 kHz mono, about 20-25 seconds of speech). They are synthetic voices
generated with Irodori-TTS: 26 with Irodori-TTS-v4.1-Anime (phasefield-audio;
MIT, a fine-tune of v4.1 Small) and 4 with Irodori-TTS-v4.1-Small (Aratako;
MIT). Each voice was designed from a text description (caption) and a random
seed; no recording of a real person was used as a reference. The ethical
restrictions of the Irodori-TTS model cards apply (do not impersonate real
people). voices/manifest.json lists them; tools/make_voice_presets.ps1 rebuilds
them from tools/voice_presets.json.

